  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 34. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 給水 — 必要な水を送り届けたり補ったりすること。\n2. 吸入 — 空気や霧などを吸い込むこと。\n3. 休養 — 体や心を休めて元気を取り戻すこと。\n4. 丘陵 — 低い山や丘が続く土地。\n5. 教育者 — 人が学び育つことに携わる人。\n6. 強化 — 力や仕組みなどをさらに強くすること。\n7. 橋脚 — 橋の途中を下から支える柱。\n8. 供給 — 必要な物などを届けること。\n9. 競技 — 決まりに従って技や力を競うこと。\n10. 競技場 — スポーツの競技を行うための場所。\n11. 峡谷 — 川が流れる深く狭い谷。\n12. 共催 — 複数の団体がいっしょに催しを開くこと。\n13. 強弱 — 強いことと弱いこと。\n14. 共生 — 異なる生き物などが関わり合っていっしょに生きること。\n15. 共通語 — 地域の違いを超えて広く通じる言葉。\n16. 強敵 — 戦いや試合などで手ごわい相手。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
